`child lump sum` `other` `paid` `dam` `n` `age` `student` MEANS
    `How much is the child's death benefit under s 59` `other` `paid` `dam` FALSE `n` `age` `student` 90000

-- s 59(4), with a made-up $90 000: 3 dependent children, a child of 10: $30 000.
#ASSERT `child lump sum` `no other parent` FALSE FALSE 3 10 FALSE EQUALS JUST 30000
-- 18 and not a student: nil; 20 and a full-time student: $30 000; 25 and a student: nil.
#ASSERT `child lump sum` `no other parent` FALSE FALSE 3 18 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `child lump sum` `no other parent` FALSE FALSE 3 20 TRUE EQUALS JUST 30000
#ASSERT `child lump sum` `no other parent` FALSE FALSE 3 25 TRUE EQUALS JUST 0
-- s 59(9): a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58: nil.
#ASSERT `child lump sum` `a parent who is not a dependent partner of the person who died` TRUE FALSE 3 10 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- The other parent is a supporting dependent partner: nil. Damages: nil.
#ASSERT `child lump sum` `a dependent partner of the person who died, who supports the child` FALSE FALSE 3 10 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `child lump sum` `no other parent` FALSE TRUE 3 10 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- No dependent children to divide by.
#ASSERT `child lump sum` `no other parent` FALSE FALSE 0 10 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

